y come  back to our communities they are coming  back better than when they left 95  percent of the people who are convicted  of an offense will come home that  includes our young people in 2018 Brave  boy launched the state's first unit to  review the sentences of people convicted  to life as juveniles it's what allowed  Arthur miles a chance at Freedom  December the 18th 2019.  and I was released to my family a week  before Christmas yes  I've been smiling ever since according  to Brave boy's office in the last four  years 40 inmates have been released  under the sentencing review unit and to  date none of them have returned back to  prison so while we get those convictions  and we hold people accountable we also  have to make sure that people have an  opportunity to be restored what did it  mean to you to have that second chance  oh man a second  a second chance  is everything  it's everything and chances may have  been what separated miles from Brave boy  we took a trip to her old high school  the same one Arthur miles attended  around the same time as Brave boy what  was so different that you became the  state's attorney and he ends up  serving a life sentence  you know  when I went to high school the  expectations were high for me I was  going to achieve there was a plan and a  path for me  so many young people at the same time  didn't necessarily have the  opportunities I had as for Miles he's  making the most of what he has now on  the weekends he cuts hair at this  barbershop it's a new life but this one  is filled with possibility are you still  in shock  um life in general  life in general I do wake up every  morning and I smile I always did have a  high Spirit but my spirit is just it's  in the clouds and now it was a  transition when I left I was a child so  now I'm learning the world  well we made multiple attempts to reach  the relatives of the victim Carl krogman  for comment and we're unsuccessful now  krogman's stepbrother said in a local  news interview earlier this year that he  believes in Rehabilitation but he  doesn't think miles should be allowed to  work in the State's Attorney's Office  calling the decision quote disgusting it  is also important to note though that  anyone released through the sentencing  review program goes through a re-entry  process which includes counseling with  needed peer groups and additional  support when it comes to finding a job  and a place to live um yeah you know  this state's attorney Aisha Brave boy  really looking at the criminal justice  system as a whole there's a number of  other things that she's done too but  this one has really been something worth  mentioning I know I keep thinking about  the victim's family though I believe in  second chances and Rehabilitation I  think if you're the victim's family  that's still very hard you said he was  16 had no criminal record no criminal  record and comes from a family that's  father was a police officer oh a police  family even it's an important  conversation to have yes it is yes and  actually said 95 of people come home  thank you Merry Christmas thank you  David thank you everybody
 

